      "content": "I understand why it feels like more work—it often is, at first, and that's brutally unfair. But the difference is that a good therapist or crisis line isn't another person to perform for; they're trained to hold your exhaustion without judgment. You don't have to explain yourself perfectly, and you can't disappoint them. The world may not change overnight, but your capacity to face it can, one small, honest conversation at a time. If you're truly at the end of your rope, please call or text 988—it's a low-effort, high-support step that doesn't require you to be anyone but exactly who you are right now.",
